IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), section 2 -- THE DEFINITIONS.
-- Layer 1: s 2(1) (the definitions), s 2(6) and (7) (the Director's determinations about "distributing
-- corporation") and s 2(8) (infants). Control, subsidiary and affiliate (s 2(2) to (5)) are in
-- cbca-core-control.l4; the individual with significant control (s 2.1) is in cbca-core-isc.l4.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Every definitional rule is named `<the defined term> within s <section>` and
-- returns TRUE when the facts it is given meet that definition. Each takes only facts a person can
-- state; where the definition turns on a judgement the Act hands to someone else, or on a document
-- outside the sources (the regulations, a provincial law, another Act), that is a plain BOOLEAN input
-- named for the fact, and the rule says so in a comment.
--
-- Definitions that are a pointer only (Director, Minister, going-private transaction, prescribed, prior
-- legislation, unanimous shareholder agreement) have no rule; see the last section and NOTES.md.

§ `Section 2 -- Interpretation`

§§ `s 2(1) affairs`

-- src:18 | affairs means the relationships among a corporation, its affiliates and the shareholders, directors and officers of such bodies corporate but does not include the business carried on by such bodies corporate; (affaires internes)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) affairs (src:18)
GIVEN `the matter is a relationship among the corporation, its affiliates and the shareholders, directors and officers of such bodies corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is the business carried on by such bodies corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`affairs within s 2(1)` MEANS
        `the matter is a relationship among the corporation, its affiliates and the shareholders, directors and officers of such bodies corporate`
    AND (NOT `the matter is the business carried on by such bodies corporate`)

§§ `s 2(1) articles`

-- "articles" is the closed list `Kind of articles` (cbca-core.l4) "and includes any amendments thereto".
-- NOTHING for the kind means the instrument is none of the nine kinds.
-- src:20 | articles means the original or restated articles of incorporation, articles of amendment, articles of amalgamation, articles of continuance, articles of reorganization, articles of arrangement, articles of dissolution, articles of revival and includes any amendments thereto; (statuts)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) articles (src:20)
GIVEN `the kind of articles it is` IS A MAYBE `Kind of articles`
      `it is an amendment to articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`articles within s 2(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of articles it is`
    WHEN JUST kind THEN TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING   THEN `it is an amendment to articles`

§§ `s 2(1) associate`

-- "associate, in respect of a relationship with a person": the question is whether ANOTHER party is an
-- associate of THE PERSON. The record states the other party's relationship to the person, one field
-- per limb of the definition.
-- src:21 | associate, in respect of a relationship with a person, means
-- src:22 | (a) a body corporate of which that person beneficially owns or controls, directly or indirectly, shares or securities currently convertible into shares carrying more than ten per cent of the voting rights under all circumstances or by reason of the occurrence of an event that has occurred and is continuing, or a currently exercisable option or right to purchase such shares or such convertible securities,
-- src:23 | (b) a partner of that person acting on behalf of the partnership of which they are partners,
-- src:24 | (c) a trust or estate or succession in which that person has a substantial beneficial interest or in respect of which that person serves as a trustee or liquidator of the succession or in a similar capacity,
-- src:25 | (d) a spouse of that person or an individual who is cohabiting with that person in a conjugal relationship, having so cohabited for a period of at least one year,
-- src:26 | (e) a child of that person or of the spouse or individual referred to in paragraph (d), and
-- src:27 | (f) a relative of that person or of the spouse or individual referred to in paragraph (d), if that relative has the same residence as that person; (liens)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) associate (src:21-27)
DECLARE `Relationship of another to a person` HAS
    `a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `fraction of the voting rights in it that the person beneficially owns or controls` IS A NUMBER
    `a partner of the person acting on behalf of the partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a trust or estate or succession in which the person has a substantial beneficial interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a trust or estate or succession in respect of which the person serves as trustee, liquidator of the succession or in a similar capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a spouse of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an individual cohabiting with the person in a conjugal relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years of that cohabitation` IS A NUMBER
    `a child of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a child of the spouse or of the individual referred to in paragraph (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a relative of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a relative of the spouse or of the individual referred to in paragraph (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `having the same residence as the person` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (a): the fraction counts shares, securities currently convertible into shares and currently
-- exercisable options or rights to purchase either, in each case carrying voting rights under all
-- circumstances or because of an event that has occurred and is continuing. "More than" ten per cent.
-- src:22 | (a) a body corporate of which that person beneficially owns or controls, directly or indirectly, shares or securities currently convertible into shares carrying more than ten per cent of the voting rights under all circumstances or by reason of the occurrence of an event that has occurred and is continuing, or a currently exercisable option or right to purchase such shares or such convertible securities,
@ref CBCA s 2(1) associate, paragraph (a) (src:22)
GIVEN `the other` IS A `Relationship of another to a person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`associate within s 2(1)(a)` `the other` MEANS
        `the other`'s `a body corporate`
    AND `the other`'s `fraction of the voting rights in it that the person beneficially owns or controls` GREATER THAN 10%

-- src:23 | (b) a partner of that person acting on behalf of the partnership of which they are partners,
@ref CBCA s 2(1) associate, paragraph (b) (src:23)
GIVEN `the other` IS A `Relationship of another to a person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`associate within s 2(1)(b)` `the other` MEANS
    `the other`'s `a partner of the person acting on behalf of the partnership`

-- src:24 | (c) a trust or estate or succession in which that person has a substantial beneficial interest or in respect of which that person serves as a trustee or liquidator of the succession or in a similar capacity,
@ref CBCA s 2(1) associate, paragraph (c) (src:24)
GIVEN `the other` IS A `Relationship of another to a person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`associate within s 2(1)(c)` `the other` MEANS
        `the other`'s `a trust or estate or succession in which the person has a substantial beneficial interest`
    OR  `the other`'s `a trust or estate or succession in respect of which the person serves as trustee, liquidator of the succession or in a similar capacity`

-- (d): the words "having so cohabited for a period of at least one year" are read as qualifying the
-- individual who is cohabiting, not the spouse (fork F5 in NOTES.md).
-- src:25 | (d) a spouse of that person or an individual who is cohabiting with that person in a conjugal relationship, having so cohabited for a period of at least one year,
@ref CBCA s 2(1) associate, paragraph (d) (src:25)
GIVEN `the other` IS A `Relationship of another to a person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`associate within s 2(1)(d)` `the other` MEANS
        `the other`'s `a spouse of the person`
    OR  (    `the other`'s `an individual cohabiting with the person in a conjugal relationship`
         AND `the other`'s `years of that cohabitation` AT LEAST 1)

-- src:26 | (e) a child of that person or of the spouse or individual referred to in paragraph (d), and
@ref CBCA s 2(1) associate, paragraph (e) (src:26)
GIVEN `the other` IS A `Relationship of another to a person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`associate within s 2(1)(e)` `the other` MEANS
        `the other`'s `a child of the person`
    OR  `the other`'s `a child of the spouse or of the individual referred to in paragraph (d)`

-- src:27 | (f) a relative of that person or of the spouse or individual referred to in paragraph (d), if that relative has the same residence as that person; (liens)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) associate, paragraph (f) (src:27)
GIVEN `the other` IS A `Relationship of another to a person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`associate within s 2(1)(f)` `the other` MEANS
        (    `the other`'s `a relative of the person`
         OR  `the other`'s `a relative of the spouse or of the individual referred to in paragraph (d)`)
    AND `the other`'s `having the same residence as the person`

-- src:21 | associate, in respect of a relationship with a person, means
-- src:22 | (a) a body corporate of which that person beneficially owns or controls, directly or indirectly, shares or securities currently convertible into shares carrying more than ten per cent of the voting rights under all circumstances or by reason of the occurrence of an event that has occurred and is continuing, or a currently exercisable option or right to purchase such shares or such convertible securities,
-- src:23 | (b) a partner of that person acting on behalf of the partnership of which they are partners,
-- src:24 | (c) a trust or estate or succession in which that person has a substantial beneficial interest or in respect of which that person serves as a trustee or liquidator of the succession or in a similar capacity,
-- src:25 | (d) a spouse of that person or an individual who is cohabiting with that person in a conjugal relationship, having so cohabited for a period of at least one year,
-- src:26 | (e) a child of that person or of the spouse or individual referred to in paragraph (d), and
-- src:27 | (f) a relative of that person or of the spouse or individual referred to in paragraph (d), if that relative has the same residence as that person; (liens)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) associate (src:21-27)
GIVEN `the other` IS A `Relationship of another to a person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`associate within s 2(1)` `the other` MEANS
        `associate within s 2(1)(a)` `the other`
    OR  `associate within s 2(1)(b)` `the other`
    OR  `associate within s 2(1)(c)` `the other`
    OR  `associate within s 2(1)(d)` `the other`
    OR  `associate within s 2(1)(e)` `the other`
    OR  `associate within s 2(1)(f)` `the other`

§§ `s 2(1) auditor`

-- "includes": a partnership of auditors, or an auditor that is incorporated, is an auditor.
-- src:28 | auditor includes a partnership of auditors or an auditor that is incorporated; (vérificateur)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) auditor (src:28)
GIVEN `it is an auditor apart from this inclusion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a partnership of auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an auditor that is incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`auditor within s 2(1)` MEANS
        `it is an auditor apart from this inclusion`
    OR  `it is a partnership of auditors`
    OR  `it is an auditor that is incorporated`

§§ `s 2(1) beneficial interest, beneficial ownership`

-- src:29 | beneficial interest means an interest arising out of the beneficial ownership of securities; (véritable propriétaire et propriété effective)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) beneficial interest (src:29)
GIVEN `the interest arises out of the beneficial ownership of securities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`beneficial interest within s 2(1)` MEANS
    `the interest arises out of the beneficial ownership of securities`

-- "includes": ownership through a trustee, legal representative, agent or mandatary, or other
-- intermediary is beneficial ownership.
-- src:30 | beneficial ownership includes ownership through any trustee, legal representative, agent or mandatary, or other intermediary; (véritable propriétaire et propriété effective)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) beneficial ownership (src:30)
GIVEN `it is ownership apart from this inclusion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is ownership through a trustee, legal representative, agent or mandatary, or other intermediary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`beneficial ownership within s 2(1)` MEANS
        `it is ownership apart from this inclusion`
    OR  `it is ownership through a trustee, legal representative, agent or mandatary, or other intermediary`

§§ `s 2(1) body corporate`

-- "includes": a company, and a body corporate wherever or however incorporated.
-- src:31 | body corporate includes a company or other body corporate wherever or however incorporated; (personne morale)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) body corporate (src:31)
GIVEN `it is a body corporate, wherever or however incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`body corporate within s 2(1)` MEANS
        `it is a body corporate, wherever or however incorporated`
    OR  `it is a company`

§§ `s 2(1) call, put`

-- One record states the terms of an option; the two definitions differ in direction, and "call"
-- excludes an option or right to acquire securities of the corporation that granted it.
-- src:32 | call means an option transferable by delivery to demand delivery of a specified number or amount of securities at a fixed price within a specified time but does not include an option or right to acquire securities of the corporation that granted the option or right to acquire; (option d’achat)
-- src:60 | put means an option transferable by delivery to deliver a specified number or amount of securities at a fixed price within a specified time; (option de vente)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) call, put (src:32 src:60)
DECLARE `Terms of an option` HAS
    `transferable by delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for a specified number or amount of securities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at a fixed price` IS A BOOLEAN
    `within a specified time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `to demand delivery of the securities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `to deliver the securities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an option or right to acquire securities of the corporation that granted it` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:32 | call means an option transferable by delivery to demand delivery of a specified number or amount of securities at a fixed price within a specified time but does not include an option or right to acquire securities of the corporation that granted the option or right to acquire; (option d’achat)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) call (src:32)
GIVEN `the option` IS A `Terms of an option`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`call within s 2(1)` `the option` MEANS
        `the option`'s `transferable by delivery`
    AND `the option`'s `to demand delivery of the securities`
    AND `the option`'s `for a specified number or amount of securities`
    AND `the option`'s `at a fixed price`
    AND `the option`'s `within a specified time`
    AND (NOT `the option`'s `an option or right to acquire securities of the corporation that granted it`)

-- src:60 | put means an option transferable by delivery to deliver a specified number or amount of securities at a fixed price within a specified time; (option de vente)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) put (src:60)
GIVEN `the option` IS A `Terms of an option`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`put within s 2(1)` `the option` MEANS
        `the option`'s `transferable by delivery`
    AND `the option`'s `to deliver the securities`
    AND `the option`'s `for a specified number or amount of securities`
    AND `the option`'s `at a fixed price`
    AND `the option`'s `within a specified time`

§§ `s 2(1) corporation`

-- src:33 | corporation means a body corporate incorporated or continued under this Act and not discontinued under this Act; (société par actions ou société)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) corporation (src:33)
GIVEN `it is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was incorporated or continued under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been discontinued under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`corporation within s 2(1)` MEANS
        `it is a body corporate`
    AND `it was incorporated or continued under this Act`
    AND (NOT `it has been discontinued under this Act`)

§§ `s 2(1) court, court of appeal`

-- The thirteen courts the definition names, one for each province or territory in
-- `Province or territory` (cbca-core.l4).
-- src:34 | court means
-- src:35 | (a) in the Province of Newfoundland and Labrador, the Trial Division of the Supreme Court of the Province,
-- src:36 | (a.1) in the Province of Ontario, the Superior Court of Justice,
-- src:37 | (b) in the Provinces of Nova Scotia, British Columbia and Prince Edward Island, the Supreme Court of the Province,
-- src:38 | (c) in the Provinces of Manitoba, Saskatchewan, Alberta and New Brunswick, the Court of Queen’s Bench for the Province,
-- src:39 | (d) in the Province of Quebec, the Superior Court of the Province, and
-- src:40 | (e) the Supreme Court of Yukon, the Supreme Court of the Northwest Territories and the Nunavut Court of Justice; (tribunal)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) court (src:34-40)
DECLARE Court IS ONE OF
    `the Trial Division of the Supreme Court of Newfoundland and Labrador`
    `the Superior Court of Justice of Ontario`
    `the Supreme Court of Nova Scotia`
    `the Supreme Court of British Columbia`
    `the Supreme Court of Prince Edward Island`
    `the Court of Queen's Bench for Manitoba`
    `the Court of Queen's Bench for Saskatchewan`
    `the Court of Queen's Bench for Alberta`
    `the Court of Queen's Bench for New Brunswick`
    `the Superior Court of Quebec`
    `the Supreme Court of Yukon`
    `the Supreme Court of the Northwest Territories`
    `the Nunavut Court of Justice`

-- src:34 | court means
-- src:35 | (a) in the Province of Newfoundland and Labrador, the Trial Division of the Supreme Court of the Province,
-- src:36 | (a.1) in the Province of Ontario, the Superior Court of Justice,
-- src:37 | (b) in the Provinces of Nova Scotia, British Columbia and Prince Edward Island, the Supreme Court of the Province,
-- src:38 | (c) in the Provinces of Manitoba, Saskatchewan, Alberta and New Brunswick, the Court of Queen’s Bench for the Province,
-- src:39 | (d) in the Province of Quebec, the Superior Court of the Province, and
-- src:40 | (e) the Supreme Court of Yukon, the Supreme Court of the Northwest Territories and the Nunavut Court of Justice; (tribunal)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) court (src:34-40)
GIVEN `the province or territory` IS A `Province or territory`
GIVETH A Court
`court within s 2(1)` `the province or territory` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the province or territory`
    WHEN `Newfoundland and Labrador` THEN `the Trial Division of the Supreme Court of Newfoundland and Labrador`
    WHEN `Ontario`                   THEN `the Superior Court of Justice of Ontario`
    WHEN `Nova Scotia`               THEN `the Supreme Court of Nova Scotia`
    WHEN `British Columbia`          THEN `the Supreme Court of British Columbia`
    WHEN `Prince Edward Island`      THEN `the Supreme Court of Prince Edward Island`
    WHEN `Manitoba`                  THEN `the Court of Queen's Bench for Manitoba`
    WHEN `Saskatchewan`              THEN `the Court of Queen's Bench for Saskatchewan`
    WHEN `Alberta`                   THEN `the Court of Queen's Bench for Alberta`
    WHEN `New Brunswick`             THEN `the Court of Queen's Bench for New Brunswick`
    WHEN `Quebec`                    THEN `the Superior Court of Quebec`
    WHEN `Yukon`                     THEN `the Supreme Court of Yukon`
    WHEN `Northwest Territories`     THEN `the Supreme Court of the Northwest Territories`
    WHEN `Nunavut`                   THEN `the Nunavut Court of Justice`

-- Which court hears an appeal is for the law of the place (outside this Act): the fact is taken as an input.
-- src:41 | court of appeal means the court to which an appeal lies from an order of a court; (Cour d’appel)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) court of appeal (src:41)
GIVEN `an appeal lies to it from an order of a court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`court of appeal within s 2(1)` MEANS
    `an appeal lies to it from an order of a court`

§§ `s 2(1) debt obligation, security, security interest`

-- "security": a share of any class or series, or a debt obligation of a corporation, and a certificate
-- evidencing either. "debt obligation": a bond, debenture, note or other evidence of indebtedness or
-- guarantee of a corporation, secured or not. Part VII (s 48(2)) defines "security" again for that Part.
-- src:42 | debt obligation means a bond, debenture, note or other evidence of indebtedness or guarantee of a corporation, whether secured or unsecured; (titre de créance)
-- src:68 | security means a share of any class or series of shares or a debt obligation of a corporation and includes a certificate evidencing such a share or debt obligation; (valeur mobilière)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) debt obligation, security (src:42 src:68)
DECLARE `Kind of security` IS ONE OF
    `a share of a class or series of shares`
    `a bond`
    `a debenture`
    `a note`
    `other evidence of indebtedness or guarantee`
    `a certificate evidencing a share`
    `a certificate evidencing a debt obligation`
    `none of these kinds of instrument`

-- src:42 | debt obligation means a bond, debenture, note or other evidence of indebtedness or guarantee of a corporation, whether secured or unsecured; (titre de créance)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) debt obligation (src:42)
GIVEN `the kind of instrument` IS A `Kind of security`
      `it is of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`debt obligation within s 2(1)` `the kind of instrument` `it is of a corporation` MEANS
        `it is of a corporation`
    AND (    `the kind of instrument` EQUALS `a bond`
         OR  `the kind of instrument` EQUALS `a debenture`
         OR  `the kind of instrument` EQUALS `a note`
         OR  `the kind of instrument` EQUALS `other evidence of indebtedness or guarantee`)

-- src:68 | security means a share of any class or series of shares or a debt obligation of a corporation and includes a certificate evidencing such a share or debt obligation; (valeur mobilière)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) security (src:68)
GIVEN `the kind of instrument` IS A `Kind of security`
      `it is of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`security within s 2(1)` `the kind of instrument` `it is of a corporation` MEANS
        (NOT (`the kind of instrument` EQUALS `none of these kinds of instrument`))
    AND `it is of a corporation`

-- src:69 | security interest means an interest or right in or charge on property of a corporation to secure payment of a debt or performance of any other obligation of the corporation; (sûreté)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) security interest (src:69)
GIVEN `it is an interest or right in or charge on property of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it secures payment of a debt or performance of any other obligation of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`security interest within s 2(1)` MEANS
        `it is an interest or right in or charge on property of a corporation`
    AND `it secures payment of a debt or performance of any other obligation of the corporation`

§§ `s 2(1) director`

-- "director" is the position, by whatever name called; "directors" and "board of directors" include a
-- single director. (The capitalised "Director" is the official appointed under s 260: see the last
-- section.)
-- src:44 | director means a person occupying the position of director by whatever name called and directors and board of directors includes a single director; (administrateur et conseil d’administration)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) director (src:44)
GIVEN `the person occupies the position of director, by whatever name called` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`director within s 2(1)` MEANS
    `the person occupies the position of director, by whatever name called`

-- src:44 | director means a person occupying the position of director by whatever name called and directors and board of directors includes a single director; (administrateur et conseil d’administration)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) directors, board of directors (src:44)
GIVEN `the number of persons occupying the position of director` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`board of directors within s 2(1)` MEANS
    `the number of persons occupying the position of director` AT LEAST 1

§§ `s 2(1) distributing corporation, with s 2(6) and s 2(7)`

-- "distributing corporation" is what the regulations define (not among the sources), SUBJECT TO the
-- Director's determinations under subsections (6) and (7). The regulations' answer is a plain input.
-- A determination is a record of what the Director found and did (pattern 8.4): s 2(6) on the
-- application of a corporation, s 2(7) for a class of corporations; both only if the Director is
-- satisfied that the determination would not be prejudicial to the public interest.
-- src:93 | (6) On the application of a corporation, the Director may determine that the corporation is not or was not a distributing corporation if the Director is satisfied that the determination would not be prejudicial to the public interest.
-- src:95 | (7) The Director may determine that a class of corporations are not or were not distributing corporations if the Director is satisfied that the determination would not be prejudicial to the public interest.
@ref CBCA s 2(6), s 2(7) (src:93 src:95)
DECLARE `Determination about distributing status` HAS
    `made on the application of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made for a class of corporations that includes the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Director was satisfied that it would not be prejudicial to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Director determined that the corporation is not or was not a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The Director MAY determine: the power is open only if the corporation applied and the Director is
-- satisfied. Whether the Director is satisfied is the Director's judgement, taken as an input.
-- src:93 | (6) On the application of a corporation, the Director may determine that the corporation is not or was not a distributing corporation if the Director is satisfied that the determination would not be prejudicial to the public interest.
@ref CBCA s 2(6) (src:93)
GIVEN `the corporation has applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director is satisfied that the determination would not be prejudicial to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director may determine on application within s 2(6)` MEANS
        `the corporation has applied`
    AND `the Director is satisfied that the determination would not be prejudicial to the public interest`

-- src:95 | (7) The Director may determine that a class of corporations are not or were not distributing corporations if the Director is satisfied that the determination would not be prejudicial to the public interest.
@ref CBCA s 2(7) (src:95)
GIVEN `the Director is satisfied that the determination would not be prejudicial to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director may determine for a class within s 2(7)` MEANS
    `the Director is satisfied that the determination would not be prejudicial to the public interest`

-- A determination takes effect only if it was made on one of the two footings and the Director was
-- satisfied; otherwise it changes nothing.
-- src:93 | (6) On the application of a corporation, the Director may determine that the corporation is not or was not a distributing corporation if the Director is satisfied that the determination would not be prejudicial to the public interest.
-- src:95 | (7) The Director may determine that a class of corporations are not or were not distributing corporations if the Director is satisfied that the determination would not be prejudicial to the public interest.
@ref CBCA s 2(6), s 2(7) (src:93 src:95)
GIVEN `the determination` IS A `Determination about distributing status`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`determination takes effect within s 2(6) and s 2(7)` `the determination` MEANS
        `the determination`'s `the Director determined that the corporation is not or was not a distributing corporation`
    AND `the determination`'s `the Director was satisfied that it would not be prejudicial to the public interest`
    AND (    `the determination`'s `made on the application of the corporation`
         OR  `the determination`'s `made for a class of corporations that includes the corporation`)

-- src:45 | distributing corporation means, subject to subsections (6) and (7), a distributing corporation as defined in the regulations; (société ayant fait appel au public)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) distributing corporation (src:45)
GIVEN `it is a distributing corporation as defined in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the determination` IS A `Determination about distributing status`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`distributing corporation within s 2(1)` MEANS
        `it is a distributing corporation as defined in the regulations`
    AND (NOT `determination takes effect within s 2(6) and s 2(7)` `the determination`)

§§ `s 2(1) entity, individual, person, personal representative`

-- src:46 | entity means a body corporate, a partnership, a trust, a joint venture or an unincorporated association or organization; (entité)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) entity (src:46)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of person or entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`entity within s 2(1)` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a body corporate`                              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a partnership`                                 THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a trust`                                       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a joint venture`                               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an unincorporated association or organization` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:50 | individual means a natural person; (particulier)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) individual (src:50)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of person or entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`individual within s 2(1)` kind MEANS
    kind EQUALS `an individual`

-- The list is closed: `an unincorporated association or organization` and `a trust` are entities but
-- are not named here, and "association" is read strictly (fork F4 in NOTES.md).
-- src:56 | person means an individual, partnership, association, body corporate, or personal representative; (personne)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) person (src:56)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of person or entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`person within s 2(1)` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an individual`              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a partnership`              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an association`             THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a body corporate`           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a personal representative`  THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The examples in the definition (trustee, executor, administrator, liquidator of a succession,
-- administrator of the property of others, guardian or tutor, curator, receiver or sequestrator,
-- agent or mandatary, attorney) are examples of the test, not extra conditions: "including, but not
-- limited to".
-- src:57 | personal representative means a person who stands in place of and represents another person including, but not limited to, a trustee, an executor, an administrator, a liquidator of a succession, an administrator of the property of others, a guardian or tutor, a curator, a receiver or sequestrator, an agent or mandatary or an attorney; (représentant personnel)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) personal representative (src:57)
GIVEN `the person stands in place of and represents another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`personal representative within s 2(1)` MEANS
    `the person stands in place of and represents another person`

§§ `s 2(1) incapable`

-- "incapable, in respect of an individual": found under a province's law to be unable, other than by
-- reason of minority, to manage their property; or declared incapable by a court outside Canada.
-- src:48 | incapable, in respect of an individual, means that the individual is found, under the laws of a province, to be unable, other than by reason of minority, to manage their property or is declared to be incapable by any court in a jurisdiction outside Canada; (incapable)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) incapable (src:48)
GIVEN `the individual has been found, under the laws of a province, to be unable to manage their property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that inability is by reason of minority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has been declared incapable by a court in a jurisdiction outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`incapable within s 2(1)` MEANS
        (    `the individual has been found, under the laws of a province, to be unable to manage their property`
         AND (NOT `that inability is by reason of minority`))
    OR  `the individual has been declared incapable by a court in a jurisdiction outside Canada`

§§ `s 2(1) incorporator`

-- src:49 | incorporator means a person who signs articles of incorporation; (fondateur)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) incorporator (src:49)
GIVEN `the person signs articles of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`incorporator within s 2(1)` MEANS
    `the person signs articles of incorporation`

§§ `s 2(1) liability`

-- "includes": a debt of a corporation arising under s 40, s 190(25), s 241(3)(f) or s 241(3)(g).
-- Those sections are encoded by other pieces; here each is a plain fact.
-- src:51 | liability includes a debt of a corporation arising under section 40, subsection 190(25) and paragraphs 241(3)(f) and (g); (passif)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) liability (src:51)
GIVEN `it is a liability apart from this inclusion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a debt of a corporation arising under section 40` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a debt of a corporation arising under subsection 190(25)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a debt of a corporation arising under paragraph 241(3)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a debt of a corporation arising under paragraph 241(3)(g)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`liability within s 2(1)` MEANS
        `it is a liability apart from this inclusion`
    OR  `it is a debt of a corporation arising under section 40`
    OR  `it is a debt of a corporation arising under subsection 190(25)`
    OR  `it is a debt of a corporation arising under paragraph 241(3)(f)`
    OR  `it is a debt of a corporation arising under paragraph 241(3)(g)`

§§ `s 2(1) mandatary`

-- "mandatary, in Quebec, includes a successor".
-- src:52 | mandatary, in Quebec, includes a successor; (mandataire)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) mandatary (src:52)
GIVEN `the place` IS A `Province or territory`
      `it is a mandatary apart from this inclusion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a successor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`mandatary within s 2(1)` MEANS
        `it is a mandatary apart from this inclusion`
    OR  (    `the place` EQUALS `Quebec`
         AND `it is a successor`)

§§ `s 2(1) officer`

-- The individual holds one of the listed offices (an `Office` constructor), or performs functions
-- similar to those normally performed by the holder of one. `holds no office and performs no similar
-- function` is the answer "not an officer". Part XI (s 125) defines "officer" again for that Part.
-- src:54 | officer means an individual appointed as an officer under section 121, the chairperson of the board of directors, the president, a vice-president, the secretary, the treasurer, the comptroller, the general counsel, the general manager, a managing director, of a corporation, or any other individual who performs functions for a corporation similar to those normally performed by an individual occupying any of those offices; (dirigeant)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) officer (src:54)
GIVEN `the holder is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the office or function` IS AN Office
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`officer within s 2(1)` MEANS
        `the holder is an individual`
    AND (NOT (`the office or function` EQUALS `holds no office and performs no similar function`))

§§ `s 2(1) ordinary resolution, special resolution`

-- "a majority of the votes cast by the shareholders who voted": more than half of the votes cast.
-- A tie is not a majority.
-- src:55 | ordinary resolution means a resolution passed by a majority of the votes cast by the shareholders who voted in respect of that resolution; (résolution ordinaire)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) ordinary resolution (src:55)
GIVEN tally IS A `Vote tally`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ordinary resolution within s 2(1)` tally MEANS
    (tally's `votes cast in favour`) TIMES 2 GREATER THAN (tally's `votes cast in favour`) PLUS (tally's `votes cast against`)

-- "a majority of not less than two-thirds of the votes cast by the shareholders who voted ... or signed
-- by all the shareholders entitled to vote". Written without division: in favour x 3 is at least
-- votes cast x 2. The first conjunct is "a majority" and matters only when no vote at all was cast: with
-- nothing cast, there is no majority (fork F2 in NOTES.md).
-- src:72 | special resolution means a resolution passed by a majority of not less than two-thirds of the votes cast by the shareholders who voted in respect of that resolution or signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on that resolution; (résolution spéciale)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) special resolution (src:72)
GIVEN tally IS A `Vote tally`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`special resolution within s 2(1)` tally MEANS
        (    (tally's `votes cast in favour`) TIMES 2 GREATER THAN (tally's `votes cast in favour`) PLUS (tally's `votes cast against`)
         AND (tally's `votes cast in favour`) TIMES 3 AT LEAST ((tally's `votes cast in favour`) PLUS (tally's `votes cast against`)) TIMES 2)
    OR  tally's `signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on the resolution`

-- src:55 | ordinary resolution means a resolution passed by a majority of the votes cast by the shareholders who voted in respect of that resolution; (résolution ordinaire)
-- src:72 | special resolution means a resolution passed by a majority of not less than two-thirds of the votes cast by the shareholders who voted in respect of that resolution or signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on that resolution; (résolution spéciale)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) ordinary resolution, special resolution (src:55 src:72)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of resolution`
      tally IS A `Vote tally`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`resolution passed as the kind within s 2(1)` kind tally MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an ordinary resolution` THEN `ordinary resolution within s 2(1)` tally
    WHEN `a special resolution`   THEN `special resolution within s 2(1)` tally

§§ `s 2(1) redeemable share`

-- src:61 | redeemable share means a share issued by a corporation
-- src:62 | (a) that the corporation may purchase or redeem on the demand of the corporation, or
-- src:63 | (b) that the corporation is required by its articles to purchase or redeem at a specified time or on the demand of a shareholder; (action rachetable)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) redeemable share (src:61-63)
GIVEN `the share is issued by a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation may purchase or redeem it on the demand of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is required by its articles to purchase or redeem it at a specified time or on the demand of a shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`redeemable share within s 2(1)` MEANS
        `the share is issued by a corporation`
    AND (    `the corporation may purchase or redeem it on the demand of the corporation`
         OR  `the corporation is required by its articles to purchase or redeem it at a specified time or on the demand of a shareholder`)

§§ `s 2(1) resident Canadian`

-- (c) reads "except a permanent resident who has been ordinarily resident in Canada for more than one
-- year after the time at which he or she first became eligible to apply for Canadian citizenship": the
-- years are counted from that time. A prescribed class of citizens (b) is for the regulations (not among
-- the sources): a plain input.
-- src:64 | resident Canadian means an individual who is
-- src:65 | (a) a Canadian citizen ordinarily resident in Canada,
-- src:66 | (b) a Canadian citizen not ordinarily resident in Canada who is a member of a prescribed class of persons, or
-- src:67 | (c) a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act and ordinarily resident in Canada, except a permanent resident who has been ordinarily resident in Canada for more than one year after the time at which he or she first became eligible to apply for Canadian citizenship; (résident canadien)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) resident Canadian (src:64-67)
GIVEN `the individual is a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is ordinarily resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is a member of a prescribed class of persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `years ordinarily resident in Canada since first becoming eligible to apply for Canadian citizenship` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`resident Canadian within s 2(1)` MEANS
        (    `the individual is a Canadian citizen`
         AND `the individual is ordinarily resident in Canada`)
    OR  (    `the individual is a Canadian citizen`
         AND (NOT `the individual is ordinarily resident in Canada`)
         AND `the individual is a member of a prescribed class of persons`)
    OR  (    `the individual is a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act`
         AND `the individual is ordinarily resident in Canada`
         AND (NOT `years ordinarily resident in Canada since first becoming eligible to apply for Canadian citizenship` GREATER THAN 1))

§§ `s 2(1) send, series`

-- "send includes deliver".
-- src:70 | send includes deliver; (envoyer)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) send (src:70)
GIVEN `it is sending apart from this inclusion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is delivering` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`send within s 2(1)` MEANS
        `it is sending apart from this inclusion`
    OR  `it is delivering`

-- src:71 | series, in relation to shares, means a division of a class of shares; (série)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) series (src:71)
GIVEN `it is a division of a class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`series within s 2(1)` MEANS
    `it is a division of a class of shares`

§§ `s 2(1) squeeze-out transaction`

-- Part XVI (cb4) uses it. The Act's "interest of equivalent value in shares issued by the corporation,
-- which shares have equal or greater rights and privileges than the shares of the affected class" is
-- one substitution that must meet all three limbs; a transaction is a squeeze-out only if there is no
-- such substitution.
-- src:73 | squeeze-out transaction means a transaction by a corporation that is not a distributing corporation that would require an amendment to its articles and would, directly or indirectly, result in the interest of a holder of shares of a class of the corporation being terminated without the consent of the holder, and without substituting an interest of equivalent value in shares issued by the corporation, which shares have equal or greater rights and privileges than the shares of the affected class; (opération d’éviction)
@ref CBCA s 2(1) squeeze-out transaction (src:73)
GIVEN `the transaction is by a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction would require an amendment to the corporation's articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction would, directly or indirectly, terminate the interest of a holder of shares of a class without the holder's consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an interest of equivalent value is substituted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the substituted interest is in shares issued by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those shares have equal or greater rights and privileges than the shares of the affected class` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`squeeze-out transaction within s 2(1)` MEANS
        `the transaction is by a corporation`
    AND (NOT `the corporation is a distributing corporation`)
    AND `the transaction would require an amendment to the corporation's articles`
    AND `the transaction would, directly or indirectly, terminate the interest of a holder of shares of a class without the holder's consent`
    AND (NOT (    `an interest of equivalent value is substituted`
              AND `the substituted interest is in shares issued by the corporation`
              AND `those shares have equal or greater rights and privileges than the shares of the affected class`))

§§ `s 2(8) infants`

-- "the word infant has the same meaning as in the applicable provincial law and, in the absence of any
-- such law, has the same meaning as the word child in the United Nations Convention on the Rights of the
-- Child". The Convention is not among the sources, so whether the person is a child under it is a plain
-- input. `NOTHING` for the provincial law means there is no applicable provincial law.
-- src:97 | (8) For the purposes of this Act, the word infant has the same meaning as in the applicable provincial law and, in the absence of any such law, has the same meaning as the word child in the United Nations Convention on the Rights of the Child, adopted in the United Nations General Assembly on November 20, 1989.
@ref CBCA s 2(8) infants (src:97)
GIVEN `whether the person is an infant under the applicable provincial law` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a child within the meaning of the United Nations Convention on the Rights of the Child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`infant within s 2(8)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `whether the person is an infant under the applicable provincial law`
    WHEN JUST answer THEN answer
    WHEN NOTHING     THEN `the person is a child within the meaning of the United Nations Convention on the Rights of the Child`

§§ `s 2(1) definitions that only point elsewhere`

-- These six definitions send the reader to another provision or to the regulations. None is worked out
-- here; each is a plain input in the piece that needs it, and the input's name is fixed in NOTES.md
-- ("Defined terms"), so that the five pieces ask for it the same way.
--   Director      s 260 (piece cb5); the capitalised official: `the Director` in Party (cbca-core.l4)
--   Minister      designated by the Governor in Council; `the Minister` in Party
--   going-private transaction     as defined in the regulations
--   prescribed    prescribed by the regulations
--   prior legislation             the Acts of Parliament that preceded this Act (used in s 267, cb5)
--   unanimous shareholder agreement   s 146(1) and (2) (piece cb3)
-- src:43 | Director means the Director appointed under section 260; (directeur)
-- src:47 | going-private transaction means a going-private transaction as defined in the regulations; (opération de fermeture)
-- src:53 | Minister means such member of the Queen’s Privy Council for Canada as is designated by the Governor in Council as the Minister for the purposes of this Act; (ministre)
-- src:58 | prescribed means prescribed by the regulations; (prescrit ou réglementaire)
-- src:59 | prior legislation means the various Acts of Parliament that were in force prior to the coming into force of this Act and that applied to the incorporation of federal companies under those Acts, other than any financial institution as defined in section 2 of the Bank Act; (législation antérieure)
-- src:74 | unanimous shareholder agreement means an agreement described in subsection 146(1) or a declaration of a shareholder described in subsection 146(2). (convention unanime des actionnaires)
